---
permalink: /ui_kits/website/children-families.html
title: Children and Youth
subtitle: From our youngest members to our teenagers, Emmanuel is a place where
  children and families are warmly welcomed into the life of the church.
intro_content: >-
  Children and youth make up a core part of our church community at Emmanuel —
  and we know how much they have to teach us about spirituality and questions of
  faith.


  On Sundays both in the Mass and through the groups we seek to offer ways for
  our young to develop on their own journey of faith. For our youngest members
  we have our Sunday 9:15 Joyful Noise Eucharist. For older children and young
  people  Children's & Youth Church take place at the 10:30 Mass on Sundays. Our
  children and young people also participate in the worship through singing in
  the choir, joining the serving team, and helping to lead the readings and
  intercessions.


  During the week we have a number of other social events with cubs and scouts
  on Tuesdays and our Stay & Play toddler group on Thursday mornings and Common
  Ground Youthgroup on Thursday evenings.
sunday_1030:
  eyebrow: Sundays at 10:30
  heading: Children's & Youth Church
  cards:
    - eyebrow: Ages 4–11 · Godly Play
      title: Children's Church
      body: Throughout term time, Children's Church meets during the 10:30 Sunday
        service. Our curriculum follows the Godly Play method of Bible
        storytelling — an approach which seeks to inspire curiosity and wonder
        in our younger members. It fosters a sense of the overwhelming love God
        has for all God's people, helping each child discover their own place in
        the story of faith.
    - eyebrow: Ages 9–11 · Up to Year 7
      title: Youth Church
      body: Youth Church typically involves some games, music and a lively exploration
        of the Gospel of the Day, or a chosen topic for the term.  Older
        children are welcome to join, but we find that by Year 7 they tend to be
        ready to join us for the service in church — singing, serving, or
        leading prayers and readings.
    - eyebrow:
      title: Forest Church
      body: 'On the third Sunday of the month, Children and Youth Church join together
        and head out into the church garden to pray, listen to Scripture,
        discover something of God in creation and respond with activities in the
        garden. '
  steps:
    - heading: Arrive & be welcomed
      body: Our children's groups meet in the church building. A welcomer will guide
        you if you or your child are unsure of where to go.
    - heading: Off to their groups
      body: Children are invited to go to their groups during the opening hymn, and
        re-join their families at the distribution of Holy Communion.
    - heading: Sign in for next time
      body: On your first visit you'll fill out a short form. If you make Emmanuel
        your church home, we'll add their details to ChurchSuite for future
        signing-in.
  room_heading: The Harold Darke Room
  room_body: Children of all ages are truly welcome at every service. For those
    who need a break, this room — next to the kitchen at the back of the church
    — has books and toys, and is specifically set aside for children under 4.
    Come and go as you need.
  room_image: /assets/cms/site-images/room-hire-1.jpg
  room_image_alt: A quiet room set aside for young children, with books and toys
sunday_915:
  eyebrow: Sundays at 9:15
  heading: Joyful Noise · Ages 0–4
  intro: Joyful Noise is our lively, informal 9:15 service for pre-school children
    and their families, with music, movement and storytelling woven into a
    short, playful celebration of the Mass. It runs during term time.
  photos:
    - image: /assets/cms/site-images/children-youth-1.jpg
      image_alt: Pre-school children taking part in the Joyful Noise service
    - image: /assets/cms/site-images/children-youth-2.jpg
      image_alt: Families gathered together during the Joyful Noise service
    - image: /assets/cms/site-images/children-youth-3.jpg
      image_alt: A child enjoying music and movement at Joyful Noise
    - image: /assets/first-communion.jpg
      image_alt: ''
  steps:
    - heading: Arrive & be welcomed
      body: Joyful Noise meets in the church building. A welcomer will guide you if
        you or your child are unsure of where to go.
    - heading: Join in together
      body: Parents and carers stay together with their children throughout — there's
        singing, movement and a short, simple talk.
    - heading: Sign in for next time
      body: On your first visit you'll fill out a short form. If you make Emmanuel
        your church home, we'll add their details to ChurchSuite for future
        signing-in.
midweek:
  - eyebrow: Thursdays in term time
    heading: Stay and Play
    body_paragraphs:
      - Stay and Play happens every Thursday in term time, 9:30 to 11:00am. This
        is a relaxed, friendly drop-in session with loads of great toys and
        usually a bit of a sing-song at the end.
      - It's a great way to meet other local parents and carers, and to get
        answers to questions about life in West Hampstead with kids. Coffee,
        toast and healthy snacks are provided, and one of the clergy or our
        youth worker is always around to host.
      - All babies, toddlers and pre-school age children, together with their
        parents and carers, are warmly welcome — with plenty of tea and coffee
        for the adults.
    image: /assets/children-families.jpg
    image_alt: Children gathered at the altar steps with clergy during an all-age service
  - eyebrow: Throughout the year
    heading: Seasonal workshops
    body_paragraphs:
      - In addition to our regular Sunday offerings, we run a number of seasonal
        workshops through the year — from our St Nicholas' workshop in Advent
        right through to Good Friday.
      - These arts and crafts workshops are open to children of all ages.
        They're great fun, and always include a suitable amount of messy craft!
    image: ''
    image_alt: ''
  - eyebrow: Tuesdays
    heading: Cubs & Scouts
    body_paragraphs:
      - The West Hampstead Cubs & Scouts group. Cubs & Scouts meet at 6:30pm on
        Tuesdays at St Cuthbert's.
    image: /assets/cms/site-images/cubs-scouts.jpg
    image_alt: The West Hampstead Cubs and Scouts group
  - eyebrow: For teenagers
    heading: Youth Group
    body_paragraphs:
      - Details to follow.
    image: ''
    image_alt: ''
school_link_label: Find details here
school_link_href: emmanuel-school.html
callout: []
---
<!DOCTYPE html>
<html lang="en-GB">
<head>
<meta charset="utf-8" />
<title>Children and Youth — Emmanuel Church, West Hampstead</title>
<meta name="viewport" content="width=device-width, initial-scale=1" />
<link rel="stylesheet" href="/styles.css" />
<style>
  * { box-sizing: border-box; }
  body { margin: 0; background: var(--paper); font-family: var(--font-sans); color: var(--ink); -webkit-font-smoothing: antialiased; }

  .cf-intro { padding: 96px var(--gutter) 100px; }
  .cf-intro .inner { max-width: 1320px; margin: 0 auto; }
  .cf-intro [data-prop="intro_content"] > p:first-child { font-family: var(--font-editorial); font-size: 30px; line-height: 1.34; color: var(--ink); margin: 0 0 30px; letter-spacing: -0.01em; }
  .cf-intro p { font-family: var(--font-sans); font-size: var(--fs-body); line-height: var(--lh-relaxed); color: var(--ink-soft); margin: 0 0 22px; }

  .cf-sunday { padding: 110px var(--gutter); background: var(--cream); border-top: 1px solid var(--line); border-bottom: 1px solid var(--line); }
  .cf-sunday + .cf-sunday { border-top: none; }
  .cf-sunday .inner { max-width: 1320px; margin: 0 auto; }
  .cf-grouphead { max-width: 760px; margin-bottom: 52px; }
  .cf-grouphead h2 { font-family: var(--font-editorial); font-style: normal; font-size: 60px; font-weight: 500; color: var(--navy); margin: 14px 0 0; letter-spacing: -0.02em; line-height: 1; }
  .cf-twocol { display: grid; grid-template-columns: 1fr 1fr; gap: 28px; }
  .cf-twocol.is-solo { grid-template-columns: 1fr; }
  .cf-card { background: #fff; border: 1px solid var(--line); padding: 40px 38px; }
  .cf-card .ages { font-family: var(--font-sans); font-size: 11px; font-weight: 700; letter-spacing: 0.22em; text-transform: uppercase; color: var(--brown); }
  .cf-card h3 { font-family: var(--font-display); font-size: 30px; font-weight: 600; color: var(--navy); margin: 10px 0 16px; letter-spacing: -0.01em; }
  .cf-card p { font-size: 15px; line-height: 1.6; color: var(--ink-soft); margin: 0 0 16px; }

  .cf-plainintro { font-size: 18px; line-height: 1.6; color: var(--ink-soft); max-width: 800px; margin: 0; }
  .cf-photorow { display: grid; grid-template-columns: repeat(3, 1fr); gap: 24px; margin-top: 36px; }
  .cf-photorow .em-well { aspect-ratio: 4/3; }

  .cf-expect { padding: 64px 0 0; }
  .cf-expect .head { margin-bottom: 40px; }
  .cf-expect .head h2 { font-family: var(--font-display); font-size: var(--fs-h2); font-weight: 500; color: var(--navy); margin: 14px 0 0; letter-spacing: -0.015em; line-height: 1.02; }
  .cf-steps { display: grid; grid-template-columns: repeat(3, 1fr); gap: 28px; margin-bottom: 44px; }
  .cf-step { border-top: 2px solid var(--brown); padding-top: 22px; }
  .cf-step .n { font-family: var(--font-display); font-size: 18px; font-style: italic; color: var(--brown); margin-bottom: 12px; }
  .cf-step h4 { font-family: var(--font-display); font-size: 22px; font-weight: 600; color: var(--navy); margin: 0 0 10px; }
  .cf-step p { font-size: 14.5px; line-height: 1.6; color: var(--ink-soft); margin: 0; }

  .cf-room { display: grid; grid-template-columns: 1fr 1fr; background: var(--paper-warm); border: 1px solid var(--line); }
  .cf-room .txt { padding: 56px var(--gutter-wide,48px); display: flex; flex-direction: column; justify-content: center; }
  .cf-room h3 { font-family: var(--font-display); font-size: 30px; font-weight: 600; color: var(--navy); margin: 0 0 14px; letter-spacing: -0.01em; }
  .cf-room p { font-size: 16px; line-height: 1.6; color: var(--ink-soft); margin: 0; }
  .cf-room .media { min-height: 280px; }
  .cf-room .media img { width: 100%; height: 100%; object-fit: cover; display: block; }

  .cf-toplinks { gap: 64px; align-items: flex-start; }
  .cf-toplinks .group .k { font-family: var(--font-sans); font-size: 11px; font-weight: var(--fw-bold); letter-spacing: 0.22em; text-transform: uppercase; color: var(--brown); margin-bottom: 10px; }
  .cf-toplinks .group ul { list-style: none; margin: 0; padding: 0; display: grid; gap: 6px; }
  .cf-toplinks .group li { font-family: var(--font-display); font-size: 19px; color: var(--ink); font-weight: var(--fw-medium); line-height: 1.35; }
  .cf-toplinks .group li .t { color: var(--brown); margin-right: 8px; }
  .cf-toplinks .group li a { color: var(--ink); text-decoration: none; border-bottom: 1px solid transparent; }
  .cf-toplinks .group li a:hover { border-bottom-color: var(--brown); color: var(--brown); }
  @media (max-width: 720px) { .cf-toplinks { gap: 28px; } }
  .cf-midweekhead { padding: 90px var(--gutter) 0; max-width: 1320px; margin: 0 auto; }
  .cf-midweekhead h2 { font-family: var(--font-display); font-size: 44px; font-weight: 500; color: var(--navy); margin: 14px 0 0; letter-spacing: -0.015em; line-height: 1.02; }

  .cf-admissions { padding: 90px var(--gutter) 0; }
  .cf-admissions .inner { max-width: 1320px; margin: 0 auto; display: grid; grid-template-columns: 1fr 1fr; gap: 80px; align-items: start; }
  .cf-admissions h2 { font-family: var(--font-display); font-size: 32px; font-weight: 500; color: var(--navy); margin: 14px 0 0; letter-spacing: -0.015em; line-height: 1.1; }
  .cf-admissions p { font-size: var(--fs-body); line-height: var(--lh-relaxed); color: var(--ink-soft); margin: 0 0 20px; }
  .cf-admissions p a { color: var(--brown); text-decoration: underline; text-underline-offset: 3px; }
  .cf-admissions .media { margin-top: 24px; aspect-ratio: 4/3; }

  .cf-schoolsection { padding: 90px var(--gutter) 100px; }
  .cf-schoolsection .inner { max-width: 1320px; margin: 0 auto; display: grid; grid-template-columns: 1fr 1fr; gap: 80px; align-items: start; }
  .cf-schoolsection h2 { font-family: var(--font-display); font-size: 40px; font-weight: 500; color: var(--navy); margin: 14px 0 0; letter-spacing: -0.015em; line-height: 1.05; }

  .cf-dbs { display: flex; align-items: flex-start; gap: 28px; padding: 40px 44px; background: var(--cream); border: 1px solid var(--line); margin-top: 8px; }
  .cf-dbs .ic { width: 56px; height: 56px; flex-shrink: 0; color: var(--brown); margin-top: 2px; }
  .cf-dbs .ic svg { width: 100%; height: 100%; stroke: currentColor; stroke-width: 1.5; fill: none; }
  .cf-dbs p { font-size: 18px; line-height: 1.65; color: var(--ink-soft); margin: 0; max-width: 56em; }

  @media (max-width: 768px) {
    .cf-intro .inner { grid-template-columns: 1fr; gap: 36px; }
    .cf-twocol { grid-template-columns: 1fr; gap: 20px; }
    .cf-photorow { grid-template-columns: 1fr; gap: 16px; }
    .cf-steps { grid-template-columns: 1fr; gap: 16px; }
    .cf-admissions .inner { grid-template-columns: 1fr; gap: 36px; }
    .cf-schoolsection .inner { grid-template-columns: 1fr; gap: 36px; }
    .cf-room { grid-template-columns: 1fr; }
    .cf-room .media { min-height: 200px; order: -1; }
    .cf-dbs { flex-direction: column; align-items: flex-start; gap: 12px; }
  }
</style>
<link rel="icon" type="image/x-icon" href="/assets/favicon.ico" />
<link rel="icon" type="image/png" sizes="32x32" href="/assets/favicon-32.png" />
<link rel="apple-touch-icon" sizes="180x180" href="/assets/apple-touch-icon.png" />
</head>
<body>

{% include "header.njk" %}

  <!-- Page head -->
  <section class="em-pagehead em-pagehead--band">
    <div class="inner">
      <div class="em-breadcrumb">
        <a href="index.html">Home</a><span class="sep">/</span>
        <a href="#">Get Involved</a><span class="sep">/</span>
        <span>Children and Youth</span>
      </div>
      <h1 data-editable="text" data-prop="title" data-type="span">{{ title }}</h1>
      <p class="deck" data-editable="text" data-prop="subtitle" data-type="text">{{ subtitle }}</p>
      <div class="meta-row cf-toplinks">
        <div class="group">
          <div class="k">Prayer Services</div>
          <ul>
            <li><span class="t">10:30</span> Children &amp; Youth</li>
            <li><span class="t">9:15</span> Joyful Noise</li>
          </ul>
        </div>
        <div class="group">
          <div class="k">Midweek Activities</div>
          <ul>
            {% for item in midweek %}
            <li><a href="#{{ item.heading | slugify }}">{{ item.heading }}</a></li>
            {% endfor %}
          </ul>
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <!-- Intro -->
  <section class="cf-intro">
    <div class="inner">
      <div class="intro-body">
        <div data-editable="text" data-prop="intro_content" data-type="html">
          {% for para in intro_content.split("\n\n") %}<p>{{ para | trim | safe }}</p>{% endfor %}
        </div>
      </div>
      <a href="service-times.html" class="em-readmore" style="margin-top:24px">See all service times →</a>
    </div>
  </section>

  <!-- Sundays 10:30 -->
  <section class="cf-sunday">
    <div class="inner">
      <div class="cf-grouphead">
        <div class="em-ornament is-leading">{{ sunday_1030.eyebrow }}</div>
        <h2>{{ sunday_1030.heading }}</h2>
      </div>
      <div class="cf-twocol">
        {% for card in sunday_1030.cards %}
        <div class="cf-card">
          {% if card.eyebrow %}<div class="ages">{{ card.eyebrow }}</div>{% endif %}
          {% if card.title %}<h3>{{ card.title }}</h3>{% endif %}
          {% for para in card.body.split("\n\n") %}<p>{{ para }}</p>{% endfor %}
        </div>
        {% endfor %}
      </div>

      <!-- What to expect -->
      <section class="cf-expect">
        <div class="head">
          <div class="em-ornament is-leading">What to expect</div>
        </div>
        <div class="cf-steps">
          {% for step in sunday_1030.steps %}
          <div class="cf-step">
            <div class="n">{{ ["i.", "ii.", "iii."][loop.index0] }}</div>
            <h4>{{ step.heading }}</h4>
            <p>{{ step.body }}</p>
          </div>
          {% endfor %}
        </div>
        <div class="cf-room">
          <div class="txt">
            <h3>{{ sunday_1030.room_heading }}</h3>
            <p>{{ sunday_1030.room_body }}</p>
          </div>
          <div class="media"><img src="{{ sunday_1030.room_image }}" alt="{{ sunday_1030.room_image_alt }}" /></div>
        </div>
      </section>
    </div>
  </section>

  <!-- Sundays 9:15 -->
  <section class="cf-sunday">
    <div class="inner">
      <div class="cf-grouphead">
        <div class="em-ornament is-leading">{{ sunday_915.eyebrow }}</div>
        <h2>{{ sunday_915.heading }}</h2>
      </div>
      <p class="cf-plainintro">{{ sunday_915.intro }}</p>

      {% if sunday_915.photos and sunday_915.photos.length %}
      <div class="cf-photorow">
        {% for photo in sunday_915.photos %}
        <div class="em-well"><img src="{{ photo.image }}" alt="{{ photo.image_alt }}" /></div>
        {% endfor %}
      </div>
      {% endif %}

      <!-- What to expect -->
      <section class="cf-expect">
        <div class="head">
          <div class="em-ornament is-leading">What to expect</div>
        </div>
        <div class="cf-steps">
          {% for step in sunday_915.steps %}
          <div class="cf-step">
            <div class="n">{{ ["i.", "ii.", "iii."][loop.index0] }}</div>
            <h4>{{ step.heading }}</h4>
            <p>{{ step.body }}</p>
          </div>
          {% endfor %}
        </div>
      </section>
    </div>
  </section>

  <!-- Midweek Activities -->
  <div class="cf-midweekhead">
    <h2>Midweek Activities</h2>
  </div>
  {% for item in midweek %}
  <section class="cf-admissions" id="{{ item.heading | slugify }}" style="padding: 90px var(--gutter) 0;">
    <div class="inner">
      <div>
        <div class="em-ornament is-leading">{{ item.eyebrow }}</div>
        <h2>{{ item.heading }}</h2>
        {% if item.image %}<div class="media em-well"><img src="{{ item.image }}" alt="{{ item.image_alt }}" /></div>{% endif %}
      </div>
      <div>
        {% for para in item.body_paragraphs %}<p>{{ para.text if para.text else para }}</p>{% endfor %}
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>
  {% endfor %}

  <!-- School Admissions -->
  <section class="cf-schoolsection">
    <div class="inner">
      <div>
        <div class="em-ornament is-leading">School Admissions</div>
        <h2>Church attendance &amp; CofE school admissions</h2>
      </div>
      <div>
        <a href="{{ school_link_href }}" class="em-readmore">{{ school_link_label }} →</a>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <!-- CTA -->
  {% for c in callout %}
  <section class="em-callout">
    <div class="inner">
      <div>
        <h3 data-editable="text" data-prop="heading" data-type="span">{{ c.heading }}</h3>
        <p data-editable="text" data-prop="body" data-type="text">{{ c.body }}</p>
      </div>
      {% if c.buttons and c.buttons.length %}
      <div style="display:flex;gap:14px;flex-wrap:wrap">
        {% for btn in c.buttons %}<a href="{{ btn.href }}" class="em-btn {{ 'em-btn--tan' if btn.style == 'primary' else 'em-btn--ghost-light' }}">{{ btn.label }}</a>{% endfor %}
      </div>
      {% endif %}
    </div>
  </section>
  {% endfor %}

  <!-- Safeguarding note -->
  <section style="padding: 90px var(--gutter) 0;">
    <div style="max-width:1320px;margin:0 auto">
      <div class="cf-dbs">
        <div class="ic"><svg viewbox="0 0 24 24"><path d="M12 3l7 3v5c0 4.5-3 8-7 10-4-2-7-5.5-7-10V6l7-3z" /><path d="M9 12l2 2 4-4" /></svg></div>
        <p>All our children and youth church leaders are DBS-checked volunteers, some of whom have professional backgrounds in education or childcare. Safeguarding the care of children and vulnerable people is taken very seriously at Emmanuel.</p>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

{% include "footer.njk" %}

</body>
</html>
